e": "Malicious GPO deployment", "type": "attack-pattern"}}, {"id": "ent_21d054e7", "data": {"title": "LSASS/NTDS dumping", "type": "attack-pattern"}}, {"id": "ent_ffe2e708", "data": {"title": "Domain-wide ransomware propagation", "type": "attack-pattern"}}, {"id": "ent_37643f37", "data": {"title": "Stopping virtual machines (pre-encryption)", "type": "attack-pattern"}}, {"id": "ent_7165115a", "data": {"title": "NetExec (nxc)", "type": "tool"}}, {"id": "ent_9a4e45cc", "data": {"title": "Scheduled task execution via SYSVOL/NETLOGON", "type": "attack-pattern"}}, {"id": "ent_a0247ce7", "data": {"title": "Domain reconnaissance", "type": "attack-pattern"}}, {"id": "ent_2f327443", "data": {"title": "Data exfiltration to cloud storage", "type": "attack-pattern"}}, {"id": "ent_442bb0ec", "data": {"title": "System profiling / host reconnaissance", "type": "attack-pattern"}}, {"id": "ent_973ccbeb", "data": {"title": "Broad Active Directory reconnaissance", "type": "attack-pattern"}}, {"id": "ent_a57b8faa", "data": {"title": "Rclone", "type": "tool"}}, {"id": "rep_3ded5086", "data": {"title": "After execution of TukTuk, the threat actor began hands-on-keyboard activity, Kerberoasting operations, and credential discovery targeting administrative accounts", "type": "report", "description": ". Next, the threat actor leveraged compromised service account credentials to deploy GoTo Resolve remote management tooling laterally across multiple systems, including servers and domain controllers. The above activity could not always be observed from the command line, but was captured in memory.\n\nOver the following days, they expanded access through RDP, SMB, WinRM, NetExec (nxc), Mimikatz, and LSASS/NTDS dumping activity while resetting privileged account passwords and conducting broad Active Directory reconnaissance. Concurrently, the actor staged and executed Rclone to exfiltrate large volumes of sensitive data to Wasabi cloud storage before deploying additional TukTuk implants across 